# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Skédio — environment variables
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev, and set each in Vercel (Settings →
# Environment Variables) for production/preview. Never commit real values.
#
# Analytics uses Umami Cloud (free Hobby plan) + Resend (free tier, 3,000
# emails/mo). You must create both accounts yourself — see Part A/B below.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── PART A — Umami tracking script (client, BUILD-time; Vite inlines these) ──
# Set these three on your Vercel project AND in your local .env.local/build.
# 1. Create a free account at https://umami.is (Hobby plan is $0).
# 2. Add a website named "Skédio" with domain skedio.studio, then open its
#    Settings tab → copy the "Website ID".
# 3. Paste it below. The tracking script injects ONLY after a visitor accepts
#    cookies via the consent banner (see src/components/CookieConsent.tsx).
VITE_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=
# Defaults to the Umami Cloud script; change only if self-hosting Umami.
# (Your script src is cloud.umami.is; the beacon posts to gateway.umami.is.)
VITE_UMAMI_SCRIPT_SRC=https://cloud.umami.is/script.js
# Only required for self-hosted Umami on a different origin.
VITE_UMAMI_HOST_URL=

# ── PART B — weekly analytics digest (server, RUNTIME; never sent to browser) ──
# Runs every Monday 03:30 UTC (9:00 IST) via the Vercel cron hit at
# /api/cron/digest and emails skediodesignspace@gmail.com.
#
# Umami API access (~dashboard):
#   1. In umami.is → your account avatar → Settings → API → "Create key" (read).
#   2. Drop that key in UMAMI_API_KEY. (Website ID is reused from
#      VITE_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID above, or set UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID explicitly.)
#   Self-hosters: point UMAMI_API_URL at your instance + /api, and either use
#   a JWT from the login endpoint in UMAMI_TOKEN or a cloud API key.
UMAMI_API_KEY=
UMAMI_API_URL=https://api.umami.is/api
UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=
# Alternative bearer token for self-hosted Umami (e.g. JWT from /api/auth/login).
UMAMI_TOKEN=

# Resend (sending the digest):
#   1. Create a free account at https://resend.com.
#   2. (Optional) Verify a sending domain, then use e.g. FROM=analytics@skedio.studio.
#      Until then, the default "onboarding@resend.dev" can send — recipients just
#      see Resend as the sender.
#   3. Create an API key (Settings → API Keys → "Create API key", Full access)
#      for RESEND_API_KEY.
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=onboarding@resend.dev
# Recipient of the weekly digest:
DIGEST_TO_EMAIL=skediodesignspace@gmail.com

# ── Cron security ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Random string ≥16 chars (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`). Vercel attaches it as
# `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` on cron invocations; the digest route
# rejects requests that don't match. Do not leave this unset.
CRON_SECRET=

# ── Sentry error monitoring (optional; free Developer plan = 5k errors/mo) ────
# Both are only read if set, otherwise everything is inert and logs as before.
#   1. Create a free account at https://sentry.io (Developer plan is always free),
#      create a project, and copy its DSN (Settings → Projects → your project →
#      Client Keys). The DSN is public at runtime, not a secret.
#   2. SENTRY_DSN (server) goes only in Vercel/local env. VITE_SENTRY_DSN is
#      inlined into the browser bundle — set it in Vercel as Production+Preview.
#   3. Server errors: anything already logged from src/server.ts + error-capture
#      is captured. Client: error-boundary failures + unhandled errors.
# Weekly digest (no code needed): in Sentry settings, add
# skediodesignspace@gmail.com as a project member; Sentry emails the weekly
# error summary automatically.
SENTRY_DSN=
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=